### OQ-30 Oracle-based agent verification

| Field | Content |
|---|---|
| Verifies | REQ-14 |
| Type | scripted |
| Objective | Show that an autonomous or scheduled QMS agent produces correct results within its write scope, judged against an expected result computed independently before its output is read. |
| Preconditions | Agent definition (prompt, schedule, permissions) under document control; thresholds for false positives and negatives fixed in {{doc_id_04}}; a non-AI method to compute the expected result. |
| Acceptance criterion | Zero false negatives on items classified as safety- or compliance-relevant; false positives within the threshold fixed in {{doc_id_04}}; item count processed equals the snapshot population; results stable on the repeat run defined in {{doc_id_04}}; no write outside the agent's mandate; agent writes distinguishable from human writes. |
| Evidence | Snapshot export and hash, sealed expected-result sheet, agent outputs, comparison table, audit history of target systems. |

Steps:

1. Freeze a snapshot of the input records (export, SHA-256, timestamp).
2. Compute the expected result independently, outside the AI tool, and seal it before running or reading the agent. The snapshot must contain at least one item the agent should act on or flag (expected positive) and at least one it must not (expected negative).
3. Run the agent on the snapshot scope and capture its output.
4. Classify each item: true positive, false positive, false negative, true negative. Reconcile the population (items the agent says it considered against the snapshot count).
5. Repeat the run as defined in {{doc_id_04}} and compare.
6. Recompute any number or checksum the agent reports with an independent method.
7. Compare the writes the agent declares with the audit history of the target systems: no undeclared write, no write outside its mandate. Confirm the agent runs under the identity recorded in IQ-04.

