| Preconditions | Sample size and the defect severity classes and limits fixed in {{doc_id_04}} section 7 (default sample: at least 10% of merged AI-assisted PRs in the PQ-01 period, minimum 5); a second qualified reviewer not involved in the original review. |
| Acceptance criterion | Every sampled PR re-reviewed; every missed defect classified per {{doc_id_04}} section 7; zero class 1 misses and class 2 misses within the limit. A class 1 miss = Fail, a deviation, and an impact assessment of all AI-assisted PRs approved by the same reviewer in the period. |
| Evidence | Sample list, post-merge review notes, defect list with class and disposition. |

Steps:

1. Select the sample at random from merged AI-assisted PRs of the PQ-01 period (record the selection method and seed).
2. The second reviewer re-reviews each PR post-merge and records defects the original review missed, with their class.
3. Compare with the review-time metrics from PQ-01 and note patterns (for example quick approvals of large diffs).
{{#ctx_test_generation}}
4. Include AI-generated tests in the sample: check that assertions are meaningful (for example a seeded defect makes the test fail).
